## Chapter 6 Discussion

In this chapter we mainly focus on possible interpretations and model comparison studies to our data, in particular the parameters extracted from the momentum dependence of the di-hadron correlation structures. First we address the Fourier coefficients and show comparison studies to other independent measurements of \(v_{n}\) from the STAR experiment. Then we compare to predictions based on initial conditions and successive hydrodynamical evolution of the system and discuss in detail the implications for QGP formation and QGP medium properties in heavy ion collisions. Finally we address the remainder parameters and discuss possible jet modifications using the remainder width behavior and comparisons to p + p data. A possible link to calculating energy transport coefficient in the QGP based on the data at high \(\langle p_{T}\rangle\) will be established. Other possible mechanisms are used to explain the remainder structure at lower \(\langle p_{T}\rangle\).

